# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages (the site is a static export: no server to set them).
#
# Content-Security-Policy: this one applies to every response, and `pnpm build` then gives each page
# its own as well (scripts/csp-headers.mjs), the same but for script-src: 'self' and the sha256 of
# each of that page's inline scripts, in place of 'unsafe-inline'. Cloudflare joins the two with a
# comma, which the browser enforces as two policies at once, so on a page only its own inline
# scripts run. A path with no page of its own (the 404 page) keeps this one alone.
#
# connect-src: the public RPCs in src/lib/cascade/config.ts (RPC), and Base Account's wallet hosts
# (*.wallet.coinbase.com). Before it connects, the Base Account SDK asks rpc.wallet.coinbase.com for
# a batch's status. Once connected, it sends every request it doesn't answer itself (a batch's
# status among them) to the RPC its popup names for the chain (the SDK's own constants give
# chain-proxy.wallet.coinbase.com), falling back to viem's default for Base, mainnet.base.org. Its
# popup at keys.coinbase.com is a window, not a connection, and its own check of the page's headers
# fetches the page itself ('self'). Browser wallets talk to the page through the extension, not the
# network. The site has no WalletConnect connector.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://mainnet.base.org https://base-rpc.publicnode.com https://archive.chain.opentensor.ai https://*.wallet.coinbase.com; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
